{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1112458-question-on-flux-intimation-and-mnemosynis","id":1112458,"title":"Question on Flux, Intimation, and Mnemosynis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-06T19:26:42-07:00","id":1112458,"title":"Question on Flux, Intimation, and Mnemosynis","content":"So, I know that the &quot;Great 13&quot; arcanoi carry with them specific visages that are displayed on the corpuses of the wraiths using them (e.g., Black eyes for those who know Argos), but are there also specific features associated with the three forbidden arcanoi: Flux, Intimation, and Mnemosynis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T23:46:58-07:00","id":1112528,"title":"","content":"Yes. According to the Wraith Players' Guide, which first introduced the three, Intimation users have their left eye turn a blazing, poisonous green, and Mnemosynis users never blink unless they choose to (yes, this does resemble Lifeweb's mark, and the Mnemoi take full advantage of it). Flux didn't get one, but Wr20 may change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:39:17-07:00","id":1112786,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you kindly marin!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T11:18:38-07:00","id":1112800,"title":"","content":"If it may help, this is in my knowledge the most comprehensive list of pre-w20 Arcanos markings, compiled from books and developer statements.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Argos: Jet-black eyes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Behest: Black lines running from hands to heart</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Castigate: Black-tinted fingers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Connoissance: A physical mark of the Shadow</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Corruption: </span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Subtle manners from the consort</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Displace: Unknown</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Embody: Dappled patterns on skin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fatalism: Symbols of fate on forehead and arms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Flux: Unknown</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Hive-mind: </span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Tumorous growths on the wraith's head</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Intimation: Left eye is bright green</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Inhabit: Red welts or burned-in traces of circuit board patterns</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keening: Musical instrument</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Larceny: </span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Corpus begins to resemble a jigsaw puzzle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Lifeweb: Eyes never close</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mnemosynis: Never blinks</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Moliate: Soft Corpus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Outrage: Bulky, knotted muscles</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Pandemonium: Peculiar mannerisms, black cloak</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Phantasm: Gossamer clothing, dramatic bearing</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Puppetry: Accents and mannerisms from former hosts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Tempest-Weaving: </span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Small cuts and scars on hands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Tempestos: </span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Scratch marks on the Corpus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Usury: Speaking in precise, numerical terms, set of scales</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Way of the Artisan: Long, thin fingers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Way of the Farmer: Aura of menace, vestigial demonic attributes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Way of the Merchant: Faint smell of incense, deceptively outgoing</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Way of the Scholar: Dignified stance, long fingernails</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Way of the Soul: Eyes glitter with supernal determination<br /> <br /> I hope a few of them get thoroughly revised by W20, since I find them unsatisfactory, especially the ones that are supposed to be represented by carrying objects (Keening, Pandemonium. Phantasm, Usury), since they seem to create annoying complications in their management. i.e. are those objects changes of the wraith's Corpus that take the form of tools or clothing, spontaneously manifesting relics, or regular soulforged or relice objects? What happens if these objects are stolen, lost, or destroyed? For that matter, what happens if a wraith uses Moliate to remove Arcanos markings? Are the markings immune to Corpus changes, or they come back after a while, and if the latter, how much?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 07-07-2017, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T11:51:51-07:00","id":1112814,"title":"","content":"Behest's is mentioned on p.163 of Wraith: The Great War, just before the Arcanos writeup - black lines running from hands to heart.<br /> Connaissance's is a physical mark of the Shadow (&quot;As a result of this intimate relationship, a Serviteur always displays a physical trademark of her Mait' Tete.&quot;, and &quot;A non-Creole wraith with Connaissance also manifests an aspect of his Shadow, usually related to the Shadow's Archetype or strongest Dark Passion.&quot;, Shadow Players Guide, p. 63.).<br /> Usury's is set to be modified in Wr20 - the Usurer's lips and fingertips are stained by life and death energies in perpetual motion.<br /> Inhabit also gets modified in Wr20, with users developing marks reflecting the objects they possess.<br /> <br /> Soulforging leaves its own mark on those who practice it in Wr20, its practitioners having some mark of the forges on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 07-07-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:24:01-07:00","id":1112835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1112458-question-on-flux-intimation-and-mnemosynis?p=1112814#post1112814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Behest's is mentioned on p.163 of Wraith: The Great War, just before the Arcanos writeup - black lines running from hands to heart.<br /> Connaissance's is a physical mark of the Shadow (&quot;As a result of this intimate relationship, a Serviteur always displays a physical trademark of her Mait' Tete.&quot;, and &quot;A non-Creole wraith with Connaissance also manifests an aspect of his Shadow, usually related to the Shadow's Archetype or strongest Dark Passion.&quot;, Shadow Players Guide, p. 63.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, thank you for reminding me, I added these to the list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Usury's is set to be modified in Wr20 - the Usurer's lips and fingertips are stained by life and death energies in perpetual motion.<br /> Inhabit also gets modified in Wr20, with users developing marks reflecting the objects they possess.<br /> Soulforging leaves its own mark on those who practice it in Wr20, its practitioners having some mark of the forges on them.[/ </div> </div> </div>Yep, I know. However I've chosen not to include known w20 Arcanos markings in the list yet for the sake of edition consistency, since previews only covered a small fraction of the Arcanoi so far and w20 shall include all of them. Let's hope just like Usury, w20 shall revise all the problematic Arcanos markings (and provide info on the missing ones). <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}